1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HUSHER, FERDINAND A. (1825-1894). BIOGRAPHY. 1 item. P 1459. The family background of a Danish-born immigrant who spent his childhood and youth in Oslo. He attended the University there and became a teacher and min
2 CONC ister in Norway before his emigration to La Crosse, Wisconsin, in 1869. He was assistant editor of Fædrelandet og Emigranten until 1973. He moved to Minneapolis and became part owner and editor of Budstikken. He returned to Fædrel
2 CONC andet og Emigranten as editor in 1975. He bought that paper in 1878 and moved it to Minneapolis in 1886. He was United States Consul to Point Stanley and St. Thomas, Ontario, Canada, 1890-1892. At the time of his death he was edit
2 CONC or of Nordmanden in Grand Forks, North Dakota. For a résumé of his career, see Norsk-Amerikanskernes Festskrift, 1914, pages 43-45.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://naha.stolaf.edu/archives/archivesguide.pdf
