1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Trygve worked in Ras Tanura (Saudi Arabia) for ARAMCO as a mgr.of constr.wrk.(oil rel.)when Erling (Henriks son) met him there in 1963.He (and wife Betty) visited Norway 1966 and T.alone several times 1966/1977-198
2 CONC (?) where he lived at Madla at brother Henrik and sister Bergit.Ret.to U.S. aprx.1986.Erling met him agn.at Tor Molaug's home in S.Fr.Cal. 1990 with his daughter Anna.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Merchant Marine and Iron Worker. Traveled regularly back and forth from California to Saudi Arabia, as an iron worker for ARAMCO.
2 CONT
2 CONT Quote from Loretta Young: "Aunt Cecile (I rarely called her Aunt Betty),  lived on Delores Street.  I forgot one of the places they lived, however, it had a huge mail floor, upstairs where she rented rooms while Uncle Ted was work
2 CONC ing in Saudia Arabia. There was a large basement where we used to dance on weekends when we did not go to the ? Hall where we danced with the Norwegian seamen Uncle Ted used to sometimes bring to the house.  I am talking 1946.  He
2 CONC  and Aunt Cecile tried to get us to marry one of them, so they could stay in the US.  I was only 16, Jean 15, and Patsy 13.  No way! One of the roomers was a woman with a daughter my age, and we would dance the Flamenco with full 
2 CONC skirts and shawls. When Uncle Ted and Aunt Cecile moved to Las Vegas, the lived down the street from Mother on Pinto Lane.  I believe the house has been demolished to make way for medical offices. They were over at Mother's a lot.
2 CONC "
2 CONT
