1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/86599700/ole-lovstad
2 CONT
2 CONT Westby, Wis. —(Special)—Last rites will be held tomorrow for Ole Lovstad, almost 90 years old. Services will be held at 1:30 from the farm home, and at 2 from Our Savior's church, the Rev. M. A. Egge officiating. Burial will be ma
2 CONC de in Our Savior's cemetery. He died Tuesday morning after an illness of about six months. Mr. Lovstad was born in Norway July 20, 1851. He was baptized and confirmed in the Balke church. Ostre Toten, Norway, where also he was mar
2 CONC ried to Kristine Oversveen, Dec. 10, 1875. They resided in Norway until 1906, when on Sept. 17, accompanied by two children, Petra and Thora, they arrived to make their home on a small farm near Westby, on which place they have si
2 CONC nce resided. Three grown children, Even, Carl and Emma, had immigrated to America ahead of the parents and had found employment near Westby. Another daughter, Marie, came to America later. One daughter, Martha, died in Norway. Sur
2 CONC vivors include Mrs. Lovstad, his wife, and children, Even, Mrs. Marie Martinson, Mrs. Nordahl Grimstad (Emma), Mrs. Edward Hanson, (Pelra), and Mrs. Oscar Villand, (Thora); and a number of grandchildren and great grandchildren. Mr
2 CONC . and Mrs. Ole Lovstad celebrated their 60th wedding anniversary in 1935 at the home of their daughter, Mrs. Edward Hanson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contributor: Mary Knothe Cooney
2 CONT
