1 OCCU Soldier, Real Estate broker
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} see the other Ralph Bergsagel entry.  This is a duplicate.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ralph grew up on his folks' farm in Bennett Lake, a farming community about 18 miles southeast of Malta, Montana. He played football for the Malta Mustangs because the coach said he had to. He worked for Buttreys Grocery Store in 
2 CONC Malta. He married Margaret Undheim in 1941, and his first son, Errol, was born in Malta, Montana in 1942. When WWII started, he joined the U.S. Army, and as a sergeant, went to Officer's Candidate School, and then entered the Logi
2 CONC stics branch. He spent most of WWII in Puerto Rico, trying to get supplies across the Atlantic to the troops there. After WWII, he was stationed in Ft. Sheridan, Illinois where Marie and Carl were born. After that he was stationed
2 CONC  at the Pentagon, living in east Philadelphia, where Louis was born, then Hopewell, then Waynewood, Alexandria, Virginia. Irene was born in Washington, D.C. before Dad was sent to Fort Richardson, near Anchorage, Alaska. On the wa
2 CONC y, he took a detour to the Army War College, and his family waited in Malta, Montana for the winter until he was done. Then the family all sailed on a troop ship to Alaska in 1959, before Alaska became a state, where they spent 4 
2 CONC years. After Alaska, Ralph was transferred to New Orleans, Louisiana where he spent two years. After New Orleans, Ralph was transferred to the Anniston Army Depot, where he spent a year as XO, then acting CO (being promoted to ful
2 CONC l Colonel) before being sent to Vietnam. After Vietnam, Ralph was transferred to the Oakland Army Base, were he oversaw the purchasing and shipping of food and other supplies to Vietnam. After 2 years in Oakland, Ralph was offered
2 CONC  a promotion to Brigadier General, with the condition that he move to the Pentagon. With 2 children in college and two in high school, Ralph decided to retire after 31 years in the Army, and move to Seattle. In Seattle he took up 
2 CONC his lifelong hobby of buying and selling real estate, and became a licensed real estate salesman, then a broker, after which he opened Bergsagel Real Estate, where he spent his second career. 
